    "message": "Dear Esteemed Family and Friends of Uncle Raj Guru,\n\nI am deeply sorrowful to learn of the demise of Uncle Raj Guru, a venerable servant of the Lord and a luminary in our spiritual firmament. My heart extends heartfelt condolences to you and your beloved family during this period of bereavement.\n\nUncle Raj Guru's unwavering dedication to his faith and his selfless service to the Lord have bequeathed an enduring legacy of love, compassion, and spiritual fortitude to many. His homilies, replete with wisdom and divine insight, continue to resonate in our hearts, inspiring us to emulate his exemplary life.\n\nI recall with gratitude the privilege of hearing him preach on Sundays during my formative years in Beulah Gardens, circa 1998, beneath the coconut leaf shed that has since been transformed into The Chapel. His messages, imbued with the anointing of the Almighty, were a source of solace, guidance, and spiritual nourishment to us as students.\n\nMay the Sovereign Lord, Who doeth all things well, envelop you with His comforting presence, grant you peace that surpasses all understanding, and shower you with His boundless love in this hour of grief. May Uncle Raj Guru's noble soul find eternal repose in the radiant presence of our Lord and Saviour.\n\nSincere and heartfelt condolences,",
