    "message": "My association with Uncle Rajaguru goes back many years, to the days when he would visit Hyderabad every month to preach. I was a teenager then, and I was privileged, on many occasions, to go to the railway station to receive him. The auto rides back were always special—he would gently enquire about my life, my studies, and how I was doing.\n\nThough he was soft-spoken, his messages carried such grace, depth, and wonderful spiritual insights. Being a professor, he connected so easily with young people and explained the Scriptures in a way we could truly understand.\n\nTo me, he was a man of prayer, marked by deep humility and a sincere passion for God’s work. His life and ministry have left a lasting impact on my heart.\n\nMay God comfort Aunty, our dear Bro. Joseph, and the entire family during this time. May His peace surround them and strengthen them.",
