    "place": "",
    "message": "Sometimes words seem so little and simply fail to evaluate a life of such sacrifice.Uncle loved my Daddy so much!He was so patient and kind to him I must say I am happy and thankful that my sister had the privilege of being his daughter in law.My first memories of Rajaguru Uncle was in Tambaram... when he would visit Willy Uncles house to teach Phoebe Akka physics...I remember what a doting father he was...and his patience with Joseph who was then the opposite of Joy.I will never forget his love and respect he had for Eddie Uncle (Joe Uncles cousin).I remember Esther saying the day they left Tambaram... Rajaguru Uncle came to our house and cried.. when we visited Rajaguru Uncle and Jeba Aunty in 2012... George was  surprised to see Eddie Uncles photos in their album.I remember Jeba Aunty saying they were our spiritual parents after we married...we had our first home in Tambaram.I must say my heart is full of joy and gratitude to see that that friendship has lasted to this day.I praise and thank god for all the families he prayed for loved.Taking note of people's names and shepherding people with prayer.It is clear for all to see Joseph his son has big shoes to step into..it is my hope and prayer that we as a church pray and shepherd him and his family that they may be a blessing to others for generations to come!❤️🙏",
