  {
    "id": "excel-tribute-209",
    "name": "George",
    "place": "",
    "message": "I remember Bro. Rajaguru during my days at the Headquarters in Chennai. He would carry his Gazetted Officer (Govt. College Professor) Stamp to help those who would need that help. He was humble, gentle and kind. Then came Annie's wedding and I remember how gently and graciously he worked, especially in connection with our discussions with my late mother-in-law, Mrs. Pramila Peter. He was very respectful and humble. He took good care of my father-in-law Mr. Peter Iqbal when he stayed at their house in Chennai. I am ever grateful to him and his entire family Sis. Jeba, Joseph, Joy, Annie and the extended family for that care and hospitality, which we were not in a position to mobilize. Peter uncle has appreciated it quite a lot. Last year (2024) I was burdened to visit him in his house. So the first thing I did after landing in Chennai was to go to my room, leave my things and go visit him. I had the privilege of spending some quality time that evening at his house. Even James Daniel told me that Peter uncle was well taken care of. You can imagine James has his own way of finding things out. I remember Bro. Rajaguru as a true man of God, who has been used of God. Our condolences to Mrs. Rajaguru and the entire family. God bless you all. 22/11/25, 07:31 - +91 90321 07000: How nice to hear the Word of God from Precious brother Rajaguru! Thank you very much for posting it. God bless you!",
    "created_at": "2026-11-11T05:13:12.189Z"
  }
